ac:1. Representative TCP and DNS fixture traffic succeeds through one authenticated SSH host for IPv4 and IPv6, and observed external addresses and resolver source match the configured exit fixtures. 2. Client UDP and TCP DNS traverse the M1 SSH DNS-over-TCP transport, cache and truncation cases behave correctly, and the physical resolver sentinel observes zero ordinary post-settings queries. 3. A reusable connection failure with multiple in-flight queries produces one atomic retired epoch, one coordinated promotion, ordered retry of eligible queries, terminal treatment of cancelled and expired queries, no per-query reopen storm, no duplicate visible answer from late old-epoch callbacks, and cache-generation invalidation. 4. Valid NXDOMAIN, SERVFAIL, and REFUSED responses never cause resolver shopping; channel-open failure, partial write, timeout, malformed or mismatched response, SSH loss, settings failure, DNS component failure, and endpoint exhaustion produce bounded explicit outcomes, mandatory teardown when required, and zero physical fallback. 5. Injected policy boundary runs cover message, in-flight, queued, aggregate-byte, and deadline admission; repeated runs reconcile runtime, packet, TCP, DNS, connection-epoch, promotion, route, and drop counters and return tasks, buffers, channels, and cache state to baseline.
