EPIC-260715-21g2pi_product-experience-and-security/STORY-260715-tx1tbz_profile-and-key-management/README.md:10:1. On iOS and macOS a user can create, validate, edit, select, and delete profiles containing display name, canonical hostname or address, SSH port, account, and a private-key reference, with field-specific accessible errors. 2. App Group storage contains only versioned non-secret profile snapshots and opaque Keychain references, is published atomically, and never contains raw keys or passphrases. 3. Imported and generated keys use the approved formats and platform cryptography, live in the minimum Data Protection Keychain access group, and are never exported without an explicit user action. 4. Deletion and replacement preserve referential integrity, handle active-profile conflicts explicitly, and remove secrets only when no retained profile references them. 5. The M1 profile loader and extension Keychain resolver consume a published generation without secrets in providerConfiguration, logs, diagnostics, or board artifacts. 6. Swift tests plus iOS and macOS UI tests cover valid and invalid profiles, import, generation, protected keys, selection, deletion, relaunch persistence, accessibility, and screenshot review.
