.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1tnjlu/TASK-260715-1tnjlu_spawn-log_-analyst--solution-architect--codex-.log:3570:.task-board/EPIC-260715-2lz67t_udp-relay-and-degraded-mode/STORY-260715-2ungml_capability-and-degraded-mode/TASK-260715-3260rm_integrate-selected-degraded-safe-dns-transport/README.md:4:Wire the approved safe-DNS upstream into degraded startup, runtime health, cache generation, and shutdown using the existing M1 DNS listener and SSH DNS-over-TCP path or the explicitly approved tunneled DoH implementation.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1tnjlu/TASK-260715-1tnjlu_spawn-log_-analyst--solution-architect--codex-.log:3573:.task-board/EPIC-260715-3810we_tcp-dns-system-vpn/STORY-260715-eto58m_vpn-manager-and-extension-lifecycle/TASK-260715-1rsqrh_implement-session-control-and-status-projection/README.md:10:1. Start requires a fresh exact-owned current enabled manager and maps every NEVPNStatus preflight/terminal row and last-disconnect result without duplicate system calls; cancellation/60-second timeout stops and never claims connected. 2. Stop is idempotent, joins connecting/connected/reasserting/disconnecting work, observes terminal status for 15 seconds, and never claims cleanup on timeout. 3. Projection preserves NETunnelProviderSession as system-state authority and current provider snapshots as capability authority; every non-connected status clears capability and missing/stale/unsupported/out-of-order facts never synthesize it. 4. Read-only v1 messages enforce 3-second timeout, request correlation, size/version/schema/generation ordering, and controller-generation retirement. 5. Tests cover every status, all public NEVPNConnectionError values, provider/unknown/nil errors, fetch timeout/cancellation, app recreation, observer/task release, start/stop races, nil/late provider responses, and fresh recovery from system plus provider state.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1tnjlu/TASK-260715-1tnjlu_spawn-log_-analyst--solution-architect--codex-.log:3610:.task-board/EPIC-260715-2lz67t_udp-relay-and-degraded-mode/STORY-260715-2ungml_capability-and-degraded-mode/README.md:7:In scope: capability bit and reason taxonomy; full, degraded, failed, and reasserting-compatible state contract; relay build and limit evidence; versioned provider snapshots; bootstrap, handshake, process, and lane failure mapping; association invalidation; deterministic degraded safe-DNS policy using the existing SSH DNS-over-TCP path or an explicitly approved tunneled DoH alternative; TCP continuity; explicit UDP and QUIC-family rejection policy input; fail-safe DNS behavior; bounded reprobe and full-mode restoration; diagnostics, user and operator documentation; state, fault, leak, harness, and physical transition tests. Out of scope: implementing TCP direct forwarding, M3 multi-lane scheduling, general path-change reconnect, includeAllNetworks fail-closed mode, captive or NAT64 transitions, final UI visuals, analytics, and silent physical fallback.
